# Docker matches these patterns from the context root, so a bare `target/` would exclude only the
# top-level one. The `**/` forms also cover a nested checkout (a git worktree's own target dir,
# database or .env). The Dockerfile COPYs only Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, src/, LICENCE and
# THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES, none of which these patterns match.
**/target/
# The redb database (file or directory) and its `.corrupt[.N]` backups hold Trakt tokens: keep
# them out of the build context.
**/metadata.db*
**/.env
.git/
.idea/
# Logs (any *.log, not just the old run.log name) — keeps stray logs out of the build context.
**/*.log
# Review-loop iteration scratch files (git-ignored, so absent from a clean CI clone, but present on
# a local `docker build .` where they bloat the context sent to the daemon). Mirror .gitignore.
iter-*.jsonl
iter-*.err
# Local git worktrees and tooling state (git-ignored or untracked, so only on a local build).
.worktrees/
.superpowers/
# Repo content the build never COPYs — excluded to shrink the context sent to the daemon.
docs/
examples/
tests/
.claude/
.github/
rclone/
about.toml
about.hbs
